    "body": "### Contributing guidelines\r\n\r\n- [X] I have read [CONTRIBUTING.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md)\r\n- [X] I have read [CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md)\r\n- [X] I have updated 'mini.nvim' to latest version\r\n\r\n### Module(s)\r\n\r\nmini.files\r\n\r\n### Description\r\n\r\n1. Cannot rename `abc` to `ABC`\r\n2. If a file with the same name exists in the directory, cannot cut and overwrite it.\r\n\r\n### Neovim version\r\n\r\n0.10.2\r\n\r\n### Steps to reproduce\r\n\r\n1. `nvim -nu minimal.lua`\r\n2. ...\r\n\r\n\r\n### Expected behavior\r\n\r\n1. Rename case sensitive\r\n2. Support shear override\r\n\r\n### Actual behavior\r\n\r\n 1. Error `(mini.files) Can not move or rename xxx. Target path already exists.` occurred while renaming abc to ABC\r\n 2. Cut `test.txt` from directory A to directory B. If Directory B contains test.txt. Error `Target path already exists.`",
